scope: |
    Two things, one file. (1) SSC3-3c cheap half, already landed as e7c456963 — register
    access through arr.get/arr.set — plus the follow-on: `build`/`run --bridge` now hand the
    bridge the OPTIMIZED module, as `exec` already did. Measured on arith-loop's loop body,
    the code that runs a million times: 47 v2 prim operations per iteration before, 32 after.
    (2) Effects across the bridge: `handle`, `perform` and `resume` translate now, both
    encodings (CPS and tail-resumptive), so all twelve v3/tests/effects fixtures run on the v2
    lane. effects-gate.sh became a differential; bridge-gate's refusal probe was re-pointed
    from `resume` to `un bnot`, the way its own comment said it would have to be.
next: land effects + optimized-module bridge, then release
